+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
 
-After selection, define the submission envelope, current-state response, unresolved-work representation, and resolution operation here. Tablet-sync will size its local storage and retry state machine around that envelope. Review-export will size its coordinator interface and export eligibility rules around the unresolved-work representation. Both must link back to this node rather than invent their own concurrency semantics.
+### Deferred
+1. Should retrieval APIs include full submission history, or only current + competing revisions? Full history may aid debugging and provide coordinators with context about how a visit evolved, but increases response size. Lean toward current + competing for primary APIs, with a separate history endpoint if needed.
+2. Should the system auto-resolve when a competing revision is identical to the current revision? Edge case (worker re-submits the exact same data after independently reaching the same conclusion), but could reduce coordinator workload. Risk: "identical" must include field ordering and whitespace, or we risk false matches.
+3. When a visit has many species entries, should the comparison UI support filtering (e.g., "show only changed species")? Unclear how often visits have >50 species and whether coordinators want to scan all entries or focus on deltas.
